    "description": "Mollie Kathleen Gold Mine Figurine Diorama\nCripple Creek, Colorado Souvenir\nAmethyst Geode, Pyrite & Pewter Figurines, 6 Inch\nDetailed mineral diorama souvenir from the historic Mollie Kathleen Gold Mine located in Cripple Creek, Colorado. Constructed on a natural purple amethyst geode matrix, this display depicts an underground mining scene accented with glistening pyrite clusters and iridescent mineral specimens. Miniature cast pewter figures of miners alongside a loaded ore cart and pine tree bring the Gold Rush heritage to life.\nNatural amethyst crystal geode formation with sparkling purple druzy cavity\nDetailed cast pewter miner figurines, ore car with pyrite, and evergreen tree\nEmbellished with brassy pyrite and iridescent chalcopyrite/peacock ore accents\nFront pewter label reads \"Mollie Kathleen Gold Mine Cripple Creek, CO\"\nMounted to a square clear acrylic base plate for display stability\nCondition:\nPewter figures, mine cart, and nameplate are securely attached with sharp cast detail. Crystal druzy and mineral clusters are intact with natural variations. Underside acrylic display stand shows glue and paper residue from a prior label. Rock matrix is solid and structurally stable with no observed cracks or repairs.\nTHANK YOU FOR YOUR PURCHASE!\nIf you’re happy and you know it, please leave a 5-star rating! If there is a problem with your order, please contact us via Shop Goodwill before opening returns/claims. We strive to return all messages within one business day.\nPlease click the shipping estimate link in the listing to get the shipping costs directly from FedEx.  There will be no discounts or price changes after an auction has ended.\nOur shipping team works hard to get out all orders as quickly as possible, that being said it may take up to 5 business days after payment for your order to ship out.  Once it ships out you will receive tracking information.\n***IMPORTANT*** If your item was damaged in transit, do not throw away anything, including the box or packing materials until we have authorized you to do so. Photos will be required to file insurance claims.\nOur Business hours: Monday - Friday  8:00 am to 4:00 pm Central\nNew items and unique treasures are added daily, come back soon!",
